<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40910" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισμῠγερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gloomy, sad</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχλύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					264
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1065
				</span></i>
			.—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has only the Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς, ἀπέτεισεν</span>
			<i>sadly</i> did he pay for it, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.195
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ναυτίλλεται</span>
			<i>at his peril, to his misfortune</i> doth he sail, <i><span class="en">
				4.672
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.616
			</span></i>.</div>
